.opencode/
dev-tools/
server/storage/
storage/
# `storage/` above targets runtime data dirs, but a bare directory pattern matches
# any directory of that name at any depth — including source. It has already cost us
# twice: element-table.cjs silently missing from releases (the parquet-ingest worker
# requires it as a sibling), and then download-trajectory-dumps.ts plus
# trajectory-not-found-error.ts never being committed at all, which left the branch
# unable to boot from a clean clone while their tracked siblings in the same folder
# hid the problem. Nothing under src/ is runtime data, so re-include all of it — the
# directory has to be re-included before its contents, since git will not descend
# into an excluded directory.
!src/**/storage/
!src/**/storage/**

.ai-workflow/
CLAUDE.md

